    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": "Grid Container and Items"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "You can turn any element into a grid by applying display: grid; to it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "html",
      "content": "1<div class=\"container\">\n2    <div class=\"item-1\"></div>\n3    <div class=\"item-2\"></div>\n4    <div class=\"item-3\"></div>\n5<div>"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "1.container {\n2    display: grid;\n3\n4    height: 150px;\n5}\n6\n7.item-1 { background-color: orange; }\n8.item-2 { background-color: lightblue; }\n9.item-3 { background-color: pink; }"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Browser Output"
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "alt": "Grid Container and Items",
      "src": "data:image/png;base64,"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Here, the element with the display: grid; rule is the grid container. The three <div> elements inside the grid container are called grid items."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Although there is no visual change yet, grid gives you access to different grid properties."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Let's explore some of these properties."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "How does it work?"
